 4. to be affected or excited, to feel passion for; 5. to be pleased or delighted with.With अनु-, 1. to redden; 2. to be fond of, to love, (with a loc.), M.iii.73; 3. to be attached, Bg.xi.36.With अप-, 1. to be discoloured, बिभ्रत्कांचनमेकमेव वलयं श्वासापरक्ताधरः Sak.vi.; 2. to become discontented with, (with an abl.), नयहीनादपरज्यते जनः Kir.ii.49.With उप-, 1. to be eclipsed, उपरज्यते किल भगवांश्चंद्र इति Mud.i.; 2. to be afflicted, to suffer calamity.With वि-, 1. to grow discoloured of soiled; 2. to be disinclined, to dislike, चिरानुरक्तोऽपि विरज्यते जनः Mrich.i., Bt.xviii.22; 3. to be disgusted with the world.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "रंज् Caus. (रंजयति-ते) 1. to colour, to paint, to redden, च्रणौ रंजयंस्त्वस्याश्चूडामणिमरीचिभिः K.S.vi.81; 2. to gratify, to please, ज्ञानलवदुर्विदग्धं ब्रह्मापि नरं न रंजयति Bhartr.ii.3; 3. to conciliate, M.vii.19; 4. (रजयति) to hunt deer.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["रञ्ज्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["raYj"]}], "ranjaka": [{"id": "raMjaka", "headword": "रंजक", "headword_slp1": "raMjaka", "fold": "ranjaka", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "रंजक (I) m. 1. A painter; 2. a stimulus.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "रंजक (II) n. 1. Red sandal; 2. vermilion.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["रञ्जक", "रञ्जकं", "रञ्जकः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["raYjaka", "raYjakaM", "raYjakaH"]}], "ranjana": [{"id": "raMjana", "headword": "रंजन", "headword_slp1": "raMjana", "fold": "ranjana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "रंजन n. 1. The act of colouring or painting; 2. colour, dye; 3. pleasing, delighting, gratifying, तथैव सोभूदन्वर्थो राजा प्रकृतिरंजनात् R.iv.12; 4. red sandal-wood.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["रञ्जन", "रञ्जनं", "रञ्जनः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["raYjana", "raYjanaM", "raYjanaH"]}], "ranjani": [{"id": "raMjanI", "headword": "रंजनी", "headword_slp1": "raMjanI", "fold": "ranjani", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "sen